    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d51">

                <pb facs="0225" n="93" xml:id="pg93"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> Leahy Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 51 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Truman to Prime Minister Churchill
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d51-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-06-05">5 June 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. Replying to your 63<anchor n="2" xml:id="d51-f2"/> and paragraph 5 of your
                        72<anchor n="3" xml:id="d51-f3"/> in regard to the forthcoming meeting, I
                    find, after full consideration, that July 15 is the earliest date that is
                    practicable for me to attend. Arrangements are therefore being perfected for me
                    to proceed to the vicinity of Berlin to arrive on July 15.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d51-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d51-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably sent to the United States Naval Attaché, London, via Navy
                    channels.</p>
            </note>
